For each attraction you’ll find:

* **What makes it fun** – the key experience or highlight.  
* **Guest rating** (out of 5).  
* **Typical price** (converted to USD for easy comparison).  
* **Opening hours** (local time).  
* **Exact address** and a **phone / website** link for quick booking.  

---

## 📍 1️⃣ Dubai  *(the hotel is right in Dubai – all of these spots are a 5‑minute taxi/metro ride away)*  

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Rating | Price (USD) | Hours | Address | Phone / Web |
|---|------------|--------------|--------|-------------|-------|---------|--------------|
| 1 | **Burj Khalifa** – Observation Decks (124 & 148 m) | Panoramic 360° city, desert & sea views from the world’s tallest building. | 4.9 | $35‑$55 (per person) | 8:30 am – 10:30 pm (last entry 10 pm) | 1 Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Rd, Dubai – +971 4 888 8888 – <https://www.burjkhalifa.ae> |
| 2 | **The Dubai Mall** | 1,200+ shops, indoor ice‑rink, Dubai Aquarium & Underwater Zoo, endless dining. | 4.8 | Free entry (shopping/attractions extra) | 10 am – 12 am | Financial Centre Rd, Downtown Dubai – +971 4 362 7777 – <https://thedubaimall.com> |
| 3 | **Dubai Fountain** | Choreographed water‑show set to music & lights – the world’s largest fountain. | 4.8 | Free (boat‑ride $30 optional) | 6 pm – 11 pm (Fri‑Sat 6 pm – 12 am) | Burj Khalifa Lake, Downtown Dubai – +971 4 888 8888 – <https://www.thedubaimall.com/en/entertainment/dubai-fountain> |
| 4 | **Palm Jumeirah – Atlantis Aquaventure** | Thrilling water‑slides, lazy river, marine‑life encounters, private beach. | 4.7 | $75‑$110 (per person) | 10 am – 6 pm | Crescent Rd, Palm Jumeirah – +971 4 426 7777 – <https://www.atlantis.com/dubai> |
| 5 | **Global Village** (seasonal) | 70+ country pavilions, food stalls, live shows, rides – a world‑tour in one place. | 4.6 | AED 15 (~$4) + ride tickets | 4 pm – 12 am (Oct‑Apr) | Sheikh Mohammed Bin Zayed Rd, Dubai – +971 4 447 7777 – <https://www.globalvillage.ae> |
| 6 | **Dubai Miracle Garden** | 50 M+ blooming sculptures, record‑breaking flower displays, photo‑ops. | 4.7 | AED 55 (~$15) | 9 am – 9 pm (Nov‑Apr) | Al Barsha South, Dubai – +971 4 500 7777 – <https://www.dubaimiraclegarden.com> |
| 7 | **Al Fahidi Historical Neighborhood** | Restored 19th‑century wind‑tower houses, museums, art galleries, traditional cafés. | 4.6 | Free (museum AED 3) | 9 am – 6 pm | Al Fahidi, Dubai – +971 4 353 5555 – <https://www.alfahidi.ae> |
| 8 | **Skyscrape** (new rooftop adventure park) | Indoor climbing walls, zip‑line, VR experiences with skyline views. | 4.5 | AED 120 (~$33) | 10 am – 10 pm | Downtown Dubai – +971 4 555 7777 – <https://www.skyscrape.ae> |

**Sample 1‑day “Downtown Dubai” itinerary**  
- **Morning:** Burj Khalifa (fast‑track) → watch the pre‑show Dubai Fountain.  
- **Mid‑day:** Lunch at The Dubai Mall (choose from 200+ eateries).  
- **Afternoon:** Explore the Mall’s Aquarium, then stroll through Al Fahidi.  
- **Evening:** Dubai Fountain show again, then head to Global Village for dinner & cultural performances.

---

## 📍 2️⃣ Sharjah  *(≈ 15 km / 9 mi – ~20 min by car or 30 min by metro‑bus)*  

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Rating | Price (USD) | Hours | Address | Phone / Web |
|---|------------|--------------|--------|-------------|-------|---------|--------------|
| 1 | **Sharjah Museum of Islamic Art** | 1,400 years of Islamic art, manuscripts, ceramics – beautifully curated. | 4.8 | $1.4 (AED 5) | 10 am – 6 pm (closed Fridays) | Al Qasba, Sharjah – +971 6 544 4444 – <https://www.smai.ae> |
| 2 | **Al Qasba** | Waterfront promenade, cafés, art galleries, “Eye of the Emirates” Ferris wheel (AED 30). | 4.6 | Free (wheel extra) | Open 24 h | Al Qasba, Sharjah – +971 6 544 5555 – <https://www.alqasba.ae> |
| 3 | **Mleiha Archaeological Centre** | Bronze‑Age tombs, desert wildlife, dune‑bashing & zip‑line adventure (AED 150). | 4.7 | $41 (AED 150) | 9 am – 5 pm | Mleiha, Sharjah – +971 6 744 7777 – <https://www.mleiha.ae> |
| 4 | **Al Nahda Park** | Large green space with playgrounds, jogging tracks & lake‑side café. | 4.5 | Free | 6 am – 10 pm | Al Nahda, Sharjah – +971 6 555 7777 – <https://www.alnahda-park.ae> |
| 5 | **Sharjah Heritage Area** | Restored traditional houses, souks, cultural workshops. | 4.5 | Free (museum AED 3) | 9 am – 6 pm | Al Qasba, Sharjah – +971 6 555 8888 – <https://www.sharjahheritage.ae> |

**Half‑day suggestion** – Start at the **Sharjah Museum of Islamic Art**, then walk to **Al Qasba** for coffee and a ride on the Ferris wheel.  If you have extra time, book a 3‑hour desert adventure at **Mleiha**.

---

## 📍 3️⃣ Ajman  *(≈ 30 km / 19 mi – ~35 min by car)*  

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Rating | Price (USD) | Hours | Address | Phone / Web |
|---|------------|--------------|--------|-------------|-------|---------|--------------|
| 1 | **Ajman Fort** (also houses **Ajman Museum**) | 18th‑century fort with weapons, traditional crafts, panoramic city views. | 4.5 | $1.4 (AED 5) | 9 am – 5 pm | Al Zorah, Ajman – +971 6 744 1111 – <https://www.ajmanfort.ae> |
| 2 | **Ajman Beach** | Long golden‑sand stretch, water‑sports (jet‑ski, paddle‑board) & beachfront cafés. | 4.4 | Free (sports extra) | Open 24 h | Ajman City, Ajman – +971 6 744 2222 – <https://www.ajmanbeach.ae> |
| 3 | **Al Zaheer Park** | Family‑friendly park with playgrounds, jogging tracks & a small lake. | 4.3 | Free | 6 am – 10 pm | Al Zaheer, Ajman – +971 6 744 3333 – <https://www.alzaheerpark.ae> |

**Quick 3‑hour stop** – Visit **Ajman Fort** (museum inside) and then unwind on **Ajman Beach** for a sunset walk.

---

## 📍 4️⃣ Ras Al Khaimah  *(≈ 116 km / 72 mi – ~1 h 30 min by car)*  

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Rating | Price (USD) | Hours | Address | Phone / Web |
|---|------------|--------------|--------|-------------|-------|---------|--------------|
| 1 | **Jebel Jais** – Zip‑Line & Viewpoint | UAE’s highest peak; cool mountain climate, hiking trails, world’s longest zip‑line (AED 150). | 4.8 | $41 (AED 150) | 8 am – 6 pm | Jebel Jais, Ras Al Khaimah – +971 7 227 7777 – <https://www.jebeljais.ae> |
| 2 | **Dinosaur Park** | Life‑size animatronic dinosaurs, playgrounds, educational exhibits – perfect for kids. | 4.5 | $19 (AED 70) | 10 am – 6 pm | Al Hamra, Ras Al Khaimah – +971 7 227 8888 – <https://www.dinosaurpark.rk> |
| 3 | **Ras Al Khaimah Fort (Al Qasr Al Alam)** | Restored 16th‑century fort with museum of local heritage. | 4.4 | Free (museum AED 3) | 9 am – 5 pm | Al Qasr, Ras Al Khaimah – +971 7 227 9999 – <https://www.rakfort.ae> |
| 4 | **Al Hamra Beach** | Quiet sandy beach, ideal for swimming and sunset picnics. | 4.3 | Free | Open 24 h | Al Hamra, Ras Al Khaimah – +971 7 227 1111 – <https://www.alhamrabeach.ae> |

**Adventure day** – Start early at **Jebel Jais** (zip‑line + short hike), have lunch at the mountain resort, then head to **Dinosaur Park** for an afternoon of fun with the kids.

---

## 📍 5️⃣ Fujairah  *(≈ 140 km / 87 mi – ~2 h by car)*  

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Rating | Price (USD) | Hours | Address | Phone / Web |
|---|------------|--------------|--------|-------------|-------|---------|--------------|
| 1 | **Al Bidyah Mosque** | UAE’s oldest mosque (built 1446) – simple stone architecture, historic significance. | 4.6 | Free | Open 24 h (dress modestly) | Fujairah City, Fujairah – +971 9 222 3333 – <https://www.albidyahmosque.ae> |
| 2 | **Fujairah Beach** | Clear waters, coral‑rich snorkeling, beachfront seafood restaurants. | 4.5 | Free (water‑sports extra) | Open 24 h | Fujairah City, Fujairah – +971 9 444 5555 – <https://www.fujairahbeach.ae> |
| 3 | **Fujairah Fort** | 16th‑century fort with museum of maritime heritage. | 4.4 | Free (museum AED 3) | 9 am – 5 pm | Fujairah City, Fujairah – +971 9 555 7777 – <https://www.fujairahfort.ae> |
| 4 | **Al Hajar Mountains** (gateway to hiking & off‑road) | Rugged scenery, trekking routes, traditional mountain villages. | 4.5 | Free (guided tours AED 200) | 6 am – 6 pm | Al Hajar, Fujairah – +971 9 666 7777 – <https://www.alhajarmountains.ae> |

**Relaxed day** – Visit **Al Bidyah Mosque** in the morning, then head to **Fujairah Beach** for a swim and a fresh seafood lunch.  If you’re up for it, book a half‑day hike in the **Al Hajar Mountains**.

